source.quote:
There exist constants $C_d,T_d>0$, depending only on $d$,
such that, for $T\ge T_d$ and scales $0<r\le s\le1/16$,
the conditions
\begin{equation}\label{eq:two-scale-upper-resources}
W\ge C_d\ell_T,\qquad
B-1\ge C_d\bigl(1+s^{-d}/W\bigr)(1+\log\ell_T)^2,\qquad
C_dr^{-d-2}\ell_T\le T/2,
\end{equation}
imply the existence of a policy
$\mathcal A\in\mathfrak A_{B,W}$ with fixed batch boundaries
satisfying
\begin{equation}\label{eq:serialized-fixed-scale}
\sup_{f\in\Lip_1(\X),\,\nu\in\Dclass(f)}
\E_{\nu,\mathcal A}\bigl[\Reg_T(f)\bigr]
\le C_d\bigl[sr^{-d-2}\ell_T+Tr\bigr].
\end{equation}
